Colb Finance is built around a simple observation: most problems in DeFi are not purely technical, but behavioral. Users are often forced to make frequent decisions under uncertainty when to rebalance, where to move capital, and how to react to changing conditions. This constant decision-making increases cognitive load and leads to mistakes.

@ColbFinance approaches this by shifting focus from continuous user action to structured financial intent. Instead of requiring users to actively manage every step, the system is designed to encode intent into reusable strategies that operate within predefined boundaries. Users decide what they want, while the protocol handles how it happens over time.

This design reduces emotional decision-making and promotes more consistent outcomes. By limiting unnecessary interaction and making behavior more predictable, Colb Finance aligns system design with how people actually use financial tools. In practice, this helps turn DeFi from an attention-intensive activity into a calmer, more reliable financial experience.

